. * rare outcome, protective effect: .05 -> .01 at n = 300 (separation matters)
. powerape dgp drare, focal(t, binary p(0.5)) baseline(0.05) nodisplay

. powerape setape drare, target(-0.04) nodisplay

. mata: ex = exact_power_sat(300, .5, .01, .05, .95, "detect", ., "fail")

. powerape power drare, n(300) claim(detect) nsim(20000) seed(8) engine(mata) n
> odisplay nodraws separation(fail)
warning: 22.4% of simulated studies had separation (a focal cell with no events
>  or no non-events, where the maximum-likelihood effect does not exist); they 
> count as failed (separation(fail), the default; Stata's probit also refuses s
> uch fits); the smallest focal cell averages 1.5 events (or non-events) per si
> mulated study; delta-method Wald inference is unreliable at this sparsity (on
> e-sided error rates can run up to about twice nominal, in the direction in wh
> ich the sparse cell has the lower rate). See help powerape, section 'Separati
> on and sparse cells'.

. mata: reca("rare .05->.01, n = 300, separation(fail), engine(mata)", st_numsc
> alar("r(power)"), ex, 20000)

. mata: st_local("sepd", strofreal(st_numscalar("r(separated)")))

